---
import { GITHUB_LABEL, GITHUB_URL } from '../lib/contact';
import { siteHref } from '../lib/site';

interface Props {
  headingLevel?: 'h1' | 'h2';
}

const { headingLevel = 'h2' } = Astro.props;
const title = 'A reporting operator who now works at dataset scale.';
---

<section class="section section--alt" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 — About</span>
      {
        headingLevel === 'h1' ? (
          <h1 id="about-title">{title}</h1>
        ) : (
          <h2 id="about-title">{title}</h2>
        )
      }
    </header>
    <div class="about__grid">
      <div class="about__body">
        <p>
          I’m Kyaw Kyaw Htun, a data analyst based in Staten Island, NY. I’m looking for entry-level data analyst roles — remote or NYC hybrid — where careful cleaning, validation, and clear storytelling matter as much as the query itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Thai Samsung Electronics I was a Channel Manager for nearly a decade (2013–2023). I built and maintained Excel- and SAP-based reports and dashboards for daily, weekly, monthly, and quarterly performance reviews across 100+ retail and distribution partners. I validated and reconciled results across sources, researched the root causes of discrepancies, and turned sales and performance trends into recommendations for senior stakeholders. I also led process-improvement work that standardized reporting and reduced report turnaround time.
        </p>
        <p>
          As a remote Sales Operation Analyst at The One Freight LLC (2024–2025), I gathered, verified, and prepared operational data for internal reports and client documentation, and entered high-volume orders, invoices, and driver logs across multiple systems — watching for conflicts and inconsistencies.
        </p>
        <p>
          My recent projects apply that same habit of checking the data before trusting it. On a 36.3-million-row NYC yellow taxi dataset I documented five validation rules, caught a missing month in the source table, and built a Looker Studio dashboard of KPI scorecards and trend charts. On 3.4 million+ NYC 311 requests I compared results across BigQuery and the Socrata API and traced zero-result errors to a frozen dataset copy and an exact-spelling mismatch.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="aside-card" aria-labelledby="about-facts">
        <figure class="headshot">
          <img
            src={siteHref('headshot-placeholder.svg')}
            width="96"
            height="96"
            alt="Neutral silhouette placeholder for a professional headshot."
          />
          <figcaption>TODO(owner): headshot</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3 id="about-facts">At a glance</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Location</dt>
          <dd>Staten Island, NY</dd>
          <dt>Work authorization</dt>
          <dd>Authorized to work in the US</dd>
          <dt>Education</dt>
          <dd>MBA, International Business School of Scandinavia, Denmark</dd>
          <dt>Certificates</dt>
          <dd>
            Google Data Analytics Certificate (Coursera)<br />
            Project Management Certificate, Stony Brook University, New York, USA
          </dd>
          <dt>GitHub</dt>
          <dd><a href={GITHUB_URL}>{GITHUB_LABEL}</a></dd>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
